Sabotage: stray 'docker run' and stray 'bwrap' additions to the non-exempt
scripts/preflight.sh, plus an unreadable scanned file; all restored immediately.
Proves: the Stage 1a exemption (scripts/spike.sh, scripts/accept/**) does not
weaken the guard, the bwrap clause is intact, and the rewritten scan fails
closed when grep cannot read a file.

## 1. docker run in a non-exempt scanned file

$ printf '\n# sabotage probe\ndocker run --rm ubuntu:24.04 true\n' >> scripts/preflight.sh
$ bash scripts/accept/0/06-no-donor-code.sh
CHECK ?/06-no-donor-code: FAIL docker run outside envrunner/, lifecycle/, scripts/spike.sh and scripts/accept/**: scripts/preflight.sh 
exit=1
$ git checkout -- scripts/preflight.sh && git diff --exit-code -- scripts/preflight.sh && echo 'exact revert: yes'
exact revert: yes
$ bash scripts/accept/0/06-no-donor-code.sh
CHECK ?/06-no-donor-code: PASS
exit=0

## 2. bwrap clause (unchanged intent) still fires

$ printf '\n# sabotage probe\nbwrap --ro-bind / / true\n' >> scripts/preflight.sh
$ bash scripts/accept/0/06-no-donor-code.sh
CHECK ?/06-no-donor-code: FAIL bwrap in first-party source: scripts/preflight.sh  
exit=1
$ git checkout -- scripts/preflight.sh && git diff --exit-code -- scripts/preflight.sh && echo 'exact revert: yes'
exact revert: yes
$ bash scripts/accept/0/06-no-donor-code.sh
CHECK ?/06-no-donor-code: PASS
exit=0

## 3. scan fails closed on an unreadable scanned file

$ chmod 000 scripts/audit-repair.ts
$ bash scripts/accept/0/06-no-donor-code.sh
CHECK ?/06-no-donor-code: FAIL cannot scan scripts/audit-repair.ts for 'bwrap' (grep exit 2)
exit=1
$ chmod 644 scripts/audit-repair.ts
$ bash scripts/accept/0/06-no-donor-code.sh
CHECK ?/06-no-donor-code: PASS
exit=0
